## Key Takeaways

- UNION attacks allow data extraction from arbitrary tables.
- Correct column count and compatible data types are required.
- Sensitive information such as usernames and passwords can be exposed through insecure SQL queries.
- Proper input validation and parameterized queries are essential to prevent SQL injection.